{"id": "DeiYDguCAOJ", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Why couldn't RAVANA's whole court move ONE monkey's FOOT? 🦶🔥 The Angad–Ravan samvad, for Dussehra.\n\nRam sent Angad, Vali's son, to Lanka to offer peace. The whole court stood up when he walked in. \"Who are you, monkey?\"\n\"Angad. Son of your friend Vali.\" \"And how is my friend?\" \"Go and ask him. In ten days.\"\n\nAngad had heard of many Ravanas: one caught by Sahasrabahu, one who lived under Vali's arm. \"Which one are YOU?\"\nRavana boasted of lifting Kailash. Angad struck the ground, Ravana's crowns fell, and Angad flung them across the sea,\nwhere Hanuman caught them for Ram.\n\nThen Angad planted his foot: \"Move it, and Ram turns back. Sita stays here.\" Warriors as strong as Meghnad rushed at it.\nIt didn't move. Ravana came down himself and bent to grab it, and Angad pulled it away: \"Why grab MY feet? Fall at\nRAM's feet.\" Ravana sat down, head bowed, his glory gone. (Tulsidas, Ramcharitmanas, Lanka Kand. In Valmiki's Ramayana\nAngad breaks the palace roof instead.)\n\n📚 Stories of our gods for your kids: Rishi Katha picture books, Books 1–3, set of 3 for ₹500 at rishikatha.com (link in bio)\n\nWhere did YOU first see this scene at a Ramlila? Comment your city 👇 Save this for Dussehra and share it with someone who never backs down!\n\n#angad #ravana #ramayan #ramcharitmanas #jaishriram #dussehra #ramlila #hanuman #lankakand #hindumythology\n#indianmythology #sanatandharma #mythologystories #kidsbooks #rishikatha", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1792114802, "like_count": 17063, "comment_count": 55, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-28593630686995335a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 69.659, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr2-2.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQNZZ2Z